🛠️ Step-by-Step: Install Certbot and Generate SSL Certificate
✅ 1. Install Certbot via Snap
sudo snap install --classic certbot



✅ 2. Run Certbot with DNS Challenge
This command will prompt you to manually add a DNS TXT record to verify domain ownership:
certbot certonly --manual \
  --preferred-challenges=dns \
  --key-type rsa \
  --email shareef391630@gmail.com \
  --server https://acme-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory \
  --agree-tos \
  -d *.kubewithshareef.xyz


You can also use -d *.kubewithshareef.xyz if you want a wildcard certificate for all subdomains.


🔍 What happens next
- Certbot will ask you to create a DNS TXT record for _acme-challenge.kubewithshareef.xyz.
- You’ll log into your DNS provider (e.g., Route 53) and add that record.
- Once verified, Certbot will generate:
- privkey.pem — your private key
- fullchain.pem — your certificate

📦 Optional: Use in Kubernetes
To use this cert in your cluster:
kubectl create secret tls kubewithshareef-tls \
  --cert=fullchain.pem \
  --key=privkey.pem


